:25 SNG7:11"},"H3724":{"lemma":"כֹּפֶר","xlit":"kôpher","pron":"ko'-fer","derivation":"from H3722 (כָּפַר);","strongs_def":"properly, a cover, i.e. (literally) a village (as covered in); (specifically) bitumen (as used for coating), and the henna plant (as used for dyeing); figuratively, a redemption-price","kjv_def":"bribe, camphire, pitch, ransom, satisfaction, sum of money, village.","n":17,"o":"GEN6:14 EXO21:30 EXO30:12 NUM35:31 NUM35:32 1SA6:18 1SA12:3 JOB33:24 JOB36:18 PSA49:7 PRO6:35 PRO13:8 PRO21:18 SNG1:14 SNG4:13 ISA43:3 AMO5:12"},"H3725":{"lemma":"כִּפֻּר","xlit":"kippur","pron":"kip-poor'","derivation":"from H3722 (כָּפַר);","strongs_def":"expiation (only in plural)","kjv_def":"atonement.","n":8,"o":"EXO29:36 EXO30:10 EXO30:16 LEV23:27 LEV23:28 LEV25:9 NUM5:8 NUM29:11"},"H3726":{"lemma":"כְּפַר הָעַמּוֹנִי","xlit":"Kᵉphar hâ-ʻAmmôwnîy","pron":"kef-ar' haw-am-monee'","derivation":"from H3723 (כָּפָר) and H5984 (עַמּוֹנִי), with the article interposed; village of the Ammonite;","strongs_def":"Kefar-ha-Ammoni, a place in Palestine","kjv_def":"Chefarhaamonai.","n":1,"o":"JOS18:24"},"H3727":{"lemma":"כַּפֹּרֶת","xlit":"kappôreth","pron":"kap-po'-reth","derivation":"from H3722 (כָּפַר);","strongs_def":"a lid (used only of the cover of the sacred Ark)","kjv_def":"mercy seat.","n":22,"o":"EXO25:17 EXO25:18 EXO25:19 EXO25:20 EXO25:21 EXO25:22 EXO26:34 EXO30:6 EXO31:7 EXO35:12 EXO37:6 EXO37:7 EXO37:8 EXO37:9 EXO39:35 EXO40:20 LEV16:2 LEV16:13 LEV16:14 LEV16:15 NUM7:89 1CH28:11"},"H3728":{"lemma":"כָּפַשׁ","xlit":"kâphash","pron":"kaw-fash'","derivation":"a primitive root;","strongs_def":"to tread down; figuratively, to humiliate","kjv_def":"cover.","n":1,"o":"LAM3:16"},"H3729":{"lemma":"כְּפַת","xlit":"kᵉphath","pron":"kef-ath'","derivation":"(Aramaic) a root of uncertain correspondence;","strongs_def":"to fetter","kjv_def":"bind.","n":4,"o":"DAN3:20 DAN3:21 DAN3:23 DAN3:24"},"H3730":{"lemma":"כַּפְתֹּר","xlit":"kaphtôr","pron":"kaf-tore'","derivation":"or (Amos 9